<comment id="121859" author="632a417d88ed2ebef97921df" created="Wed, 16 Apr 2025 11:45:02 -0500"><p><a href="https://lspapp.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=5f80cd5758899e0070c0fdd8" class="user-hover" rel="5f80cd5758899e0070c0fdd8" data-account-id="5f80cd5758899e0070c0fdd8" accountid="5f80cd5758899e0070c0fdd8" rel="noreferrer">Brynn Reilly</a> - heads up the LSC is requesting to be compensated for issues caused by this - I know 7.6 is likely impossible at this point, but we should prioritize this as is possible, so we don’t have to keep paying them out for it. Thank you! cc <a href="https://lspapp.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A1b8a895e-7d7c-4fd5-bf83-4537a643a45c" class="user-hover" rel="712020:1b8a895e-7d7c-4fd5-bf83-4537a643a45c" data-account-id="712020:1b8a895e-7d7c-4fd5-bf83-4537a643a45c" accountid="712020:1b8a895e-7d7c-4fd5-bf83-4537a643a45c" rel="noreferrer">Trent Bauer</a> </p></comment>
<comment id="122963" author="557058:bf72cd80-5754-4e78-9de4-bed28880e058" created="Fri, 9 May 2025 06:50:51 -0500"><p>I can’t reproduce this issue, but may be customer has admins, which don’t meet criteria to be notification recipients. So we send appointment notifications to LSC default and custom admins if they satisfy following conditions:</p> <ol> <li>They assigned to role, which has Manage access to appointments (in Configuration → Company → Roles).</li> <li>They are watchers of Account, which appointment belongs to. So they should be in following list:<br/> <span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="/rest/api/3/attachment/content/53429" alt="image-20250509-114644.png" height="499" width="512" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span></li> </ol> <p>Otherwise they are not being notified according to our general rules. I highly suspect customer’s admins just don’t fit for that <a href="https://lspapp.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=632a417d88ed2ebef97921df" class="user-hover" rel="632a417d88ed2ebef97921df" data-account-id="632a417d88ed2ebef97921df" accountid="632a417d88ed2ebef97921df" rel="noreferrer">Austen Brockman</a>.</p> <p><a href="https://lspapp.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A79c4f308-8b73-492a-8707-3c2bca52afe7" class="user-hover" rel="712020:79c4f308-8b73-492a-8707-3c2bca52afe7" data-account-id="712020:79c4f308-8b73-492a-8707-3c2bca52afe7" accountid="712020:79c4f308-8b73-492a-8707-3c2bca52afe7" rel="noreferrer">Jake Orona</a> could you please check if you are not able to repro the issue with admins meeting those critera above?</p></comment>
<comment id="123075" author="712020:79c4f308-8b73-492a-8707-3c2bca52afe7" created="Mon, 12 May 2025 13:25:11 -0500"><p><a href="https://lspapp.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3Abf72cd80-5754-4e78-9de4-bed28880e058" class="user-hover" rel="557058:bf72cd80-5754-4e78-9de4-bed28880e058" data-account-id="557058:bf72cd80-5754-4e78-9de4-bed28880e058" accountid="557058:bf72cd80-5754-4e78-9de4-bed28880e058" rel="noreferrer">Pavel Savrovsky</a> Retested on QA and Staging with “Time Revised by Interpreter” and “Interpreter Unassigned” emails.</p> <p><b>QA Env:</b></p> <p>I am unable to reproduce the issue on QA when the Admin is a watcher of the account (Root, Default &amp; Custom). I also tested “Interpreter Unassigned“ emails for <a href="https://lspapp.atlassian.net/browse/PP-8453" title="smart-link" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://lspapp.atlassian.net/browse/PP-8453</a> .</p> <ul> <li>QA Credentials: <ul> <li>Root LSC Admin #1: <a href="mailto:jake-qadev@interpretmanager.com" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">jake-qadev@interpretmanager.com</a> / Whitney1!</li> <li>Root LSC Admin #2: <a href="mailto:jakeqabl+bobradmin@gmail.com" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">jakeqabl+bobradmin@gmail.com</a> / Boostie@qa1!</li> <li>Account: 3rd Company <ul> <li>Both LSC Root Admins are watchers for the account</li> </ul> </li> </ul> </li> </ul> <p><b>Staging Env:</b></p> <p>I am able to reproduce the issue on Staging when the Admin is a watcher of the account (Root, Default &amp; Custom) for both “Time Revised by Interpreter” and “Interpreter Unassigned” emails.</p> <ul> <li>Staging Credentials: <ul> <li>Root LSC Admin #1: <a href="mailto:jake-qadev@interpretmanager.com" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">jake-qadev@interpretmanager.com</a> / Whitney1!</li> <li>Root LSC Admin #2: <a href="mailto:jakeqabl+bobradmin@gmail.com" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">jakeqabl+bobradmin@gmail.com</a> / Boostie@qa1!</li> <li>Account: Suppressed Light <ul> <li>Both LSC Root Admins are watchers for the account</li> </ul> </li> </ul> </li> </ul> </comment>
<comment id="123700" author="557058:bf72cd80-5754-4e78-9de4-bed28880e058" created="Wed, 21 May 2025 08:01:47 -0500"><p>Hey <a href="https://lspapp.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A79c4f308-8b73-492a-8707-3c2bca52afe7" class="user-hover" rel="712020:79c4f308-8b73-492a-8707-3c2bca52afe7" data-account-id="712020:79c4f308-8b73-492a-8707-3c2bca52afe7" accountid="712020:79c4f308-8b73-492a-8707-3c2bca52afe7" rel="noreferrer">Jake Orona</a>! I’m still unable to reproduce issues anywhere, so could you please check following points for your cases on staging:</p> <ol> <li>Regarding Interpreter Unassigned notification, please look into my comment in <a href="https://lspapp.atlassian.net/browse/PP-8453" title="smart-link" class="external-link" rel="nofollow noreferrer">https://lspapp.atlassian.net/browse/PP-8453</a> and check if this is your case either or not. So if you unassign interpreter, which is already scheduled, notification is driven by another Scheduled Interpreter Unassigned group in settings:</li> </ol> <p><span class="image-wrap" style=""><img src="/rest/api/3/attachment/content/53770" alt="image-20250521-125536.png" height="428" width="786" style="border: 0px solid black" /></span><br/> I see you don’t have root LSC admin here, so he won’t get email in this case.</p> <ol> <li>Regarding Time Revised by Interpreter, I’m not sure, but is this possible you did wrong revise action for that? Please note that notification won’t be raised if you revise as admin - it’s only for non-admin interpreter action.</li> </ol> <p>If you are still able to reproduce any of these, could you please share appointment id, so I would dig into it more?</p></comment>
<comment id="125809" author="712020:8611a661-a86c-41f2-9e3c-a84b8034a6ef" created="Mon, 23 Jun 2025 06:33:03 -0500"><p><a href="https://lspapp.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=557058%3Abf72cd80-5754-4e78-9de4-bed28880e058" class="user-hover" rel="557058:bf72cd80-5754-4e78-9de4-bed28880e058" data-account-id="557058:bf72cd80-5754-4e78-9de4-bed28880e058" accountid="557058:bf72cd80-5754-4e78-9de4-bed28880e058" rel="noreferrer">Pavel Savrovsky</a> <a href="https://lspapp.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A79c4f308-8b73-492a-8707-3c2bca52afe7" class="user-hover" rel="712020:79c4f308-8b73-492a-8707-3c2bca52afe7" data-account-id="712020:79c4f308-8b73-492a-8707-3c2bca52afe7" accountid="712020:79c4f308-8b73-492a-8707-3c2bca52afe7" rel="noreferrer">Jake Orona</a> I tested this multiple times on QA and I’m not able to reproduce the issue. I’m receiving “Time Revised by Interpreter” notifications as Default Administrator and Default Requestor Administrator when the conditions Pavel mentioned below are met. How should we proceed with this?</p></comment>
<comment id="126451" author="712020:abf08299-1d05-45de-96ba-0393d8a819b4" created="Tue, 1 Jul 2025 10:48:36 -0500"><p><a href="https://lspapp.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=712020%3A79c4f308-8b73-492a-8707-3c2bca52afe7" class="user-hover" rel="712020:79c4f308-8b73-492a-8707-3c2bca52afe7" data-account-id="712020:79c4f308-8b73-492a-8707-3c2bca52afe7" accountid="712020:79c4f308-8b73-492a-8707-3c2bca52afe7" rel="noreferrer">Jake Orona</a> when you’re back, can you attempt to retest once more?</p> <p>If not reproducible, let’s close! </p></comment>
</comments>
